 "text": "9/29/26, 9:42 AM\ne Qe= Estimated Quantity\n\ne = Gas Factor\n\nMR,                E>                 E                                    MR,\nOQ, \u00ae,\n\nExample 4\n\nIn example 4, interpolation takes place between the estimated meter readings MRO and MRI. The system uses the (averaged)\nfactor \u00ae from the period MRO to MRI in all steps for the conversion between meter reading and consumption. This ensures that\nthe total consumption Q is retained:\n\nQ= Qe+ Ql.\n\nIf another meter reading is subsequently estimated between MRO and E, the system uses the averaged factor Ye from the period\nMR1 to E for the conversion between the meter readings and consumption values. However, as the factors \u00ae and \u00aee are generally\n\ndifferent, the total consumption Q is not retained.\n\nInteraction - Estimation and Actual Meter Reading\n\nUse\n\nOne feature of the quantity determination procedure Quantity Determination During Meter Reading for the gas division is the way\nin which the quantity is calculated once an actual meter reading is available following one or more estimations (usually\n\nextrapolations).\n\nFeatures\n\nIn this case, to harmonize the results, the gas factors are determined for the most recent actual previous meter reading result. The\n\nsystem calculates the quantity as follows:\n\nQ, = (MR, - E,) * 0;\n\nFormula\n\nThis is explained in the following figure.\n",
